{"type":"message","id":"93d04e3a","parentId":"caf5a5b5","timestamp":"2026-07-28T13:04:12.138Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"So the database exists and has feed_jobs table, but I don't see a job with feed_id matching `feed-drain-coinography-20260728-130112`. The feed_jobs have feed_ids like `f-coinography-20260728-111804`.\n\nLooking at the cron message again: `[cron:616205ef-53d0-4ebb-b2bd-31a396f18610 feed-drain-coinography-20260728-130112]`. This looks like maybe `616205ef-53d0-4ebb-b2bd-31a396f18610` is the cron ID and `feed-drain-coinography-20260728-130112` is some identifier.\n\nActually, let me think about this differently. The FEED_DRAIN is coming from a cron job. Looking at SOUL.md routing, it says \"Feed drain entry (use `--feed-job-id`)\". But looking at the build_picker_input.py script, it expects an integer job ID.\n\nMaybe I'm misunderstanding the flow. Let me check if there's a different script for FEED_DRAIN or if I should be using a different approach.\n\nLet me check the actual cron message format more carefully. The message shows `[cron:616205ef-53d0-4ebb-b2bd-31a396f18610 feed-drain-coinography-20260728-130112]` at the beginning. This looks like a cron identifier. The actual content is `FEED_DRAIN {\"project\": \"coinography\"}`.\n\nMaybe I need to parse this as JSON and handle it differently. Let me check if there's a feed-drain specific handler:\n\n<｜DSML｜function_calls"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_57e7f9759e0644f69d102880","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"source /tmp/coinography-run-env.sh && python3 -c \"\nimport json\nimport re\n\nmessage = '[cron:616205ef-53d0-4ebb-b2bd-31a396f18610 feed-drain-coinography-20260728-130112] FEED_DRAIN {\\\"project\\\": \\\"coinography\\\"}'\nprint('Full message:', message)\n\n# Try to extract JSON part\nmatch = re.search(r'FEED_DRAIN\\s+({.+})', message)\nif match:\n    json_str = match.group(1)\n    print('Extracted JSON:', json_str)\n    try:\n        data = json.loads(json_str)\n        print('Parsed data:', data)\n        print('Project:', data.get('project'))\n    except json.JSONDecodeError as e:\n        print('JSON decode error:', e)\n\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bedrock-mantle","model":"deepseek.v3.2","usage":{"input":25748,"output":584,"cacheRead":576,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":26908,"cost":{"input":0.01647872,"output":0.0011154399999999999,"cacheRead":0.00009216,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01768632}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1785243843014,"responseId":"chatcmpl-152832bd-01f6-4ac5-8282-0cf359ef3fcd"}}
